# SSH client configuration
#
# Managed by dotfiles (stow package: ssh). Stow links this file individually
# into ~/.ssh/, so id_rsa, known_hosts and authorized_keys remain real,
# untracked files. Never add keys or known_hosts to this package.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Idle-connection keepalive
#
# Without this, an idle session dies silently: a stateful middlebox on the
# path (carrier-grade NAT, campus firewall) evicts the flow's state entry
# after ~60-120s of silence and sends no RST, so both endpoints still believe
# the connection is open. The next keystroke vanishes into a black hole and
# the terminal appears frozen until the TCP retransmit backoff finally
# expires, minutes later.
#
# Observed on adam -> 140.164.12.64 (2026-09-11): a wedged session showed
# backoff:10, retrans:1/11, cwnd:1, rto:120000, lastrcv 580s with lastsnd 68s
# -- eleven unacknowledged retransmissions of a 288-byte Send-Q, strictly
# one-directional traffic.
#
# TCPKeepAlive alone cannot prevent this: net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_time is 7200,
# so the kernel's first probe arrives two hours in. ServerAliveInterval is the
# load-bearing setting -- it sends an encrypted SSH-level ping every 30s,
# keeping the middlebox state entry fresh.
#
# 30s x 6 = the client gives up after ~3 minutes of a genuinely dead path,
# rather than hanging indefinitely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Host *
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    ServerAliveCountMax 6
    TCPKeepAlive yes

